<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy — FreeMCP" description="How FreeMCP handles information provided through the website and linked services.">
<article class="container info-page"><div class="eyebrow">FREEMCP / INFORMATION</div><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="intro">How FreeMCP handles information provided through the website and linked services.</p><div class="info-content"><p><strong>Last updated:</strong> 22 November 2026</p><p>This policy explains how information may be processed when you browse FreeMCP, submit a listing, or follow links to external services.</p><h2>Information you choose to provide</h2><p>When you submit a server, the information you enter may be included in a public GitHub issue and, if approved, in a public registry listing. Do not submit credentials, confidential data, or information you do not have permission to share.</p><h2>Technical information</h2><p>Our hosting and infrastructure providers may process request metadata such as IP addresses, browser information, and access logs to operate and protect the site. Retention and processing depend on the provider configuration.</p><h2>External services</h2><p>Links to GitHub, maintainer websites, and third-party sponsorship or payment platforms take you to services governed by their own privacy policies. FreeMCP may display promotional placements.</p><h2>Analytics and cookies</h2><p>FreeMCP uses browser localStorage to remember your light or dark theme preference and sessionStorage to temporarily cache GitHub repository metadata on server detail pages. These browser storage features are not HTTP cookies. In a homepage response-header check on 22 November 2026, no Set-Cookie header was observed; this check does not establish the behavior of every page or third-party service. If optional analytics or advertising tracking is introduced, this policy and any applicable consent choices will be updated.</p><h2>Requests and contact</h2><p>For questions or requests concerning registry information, contact <a href="mailto:agents@freemcp.in">agents@freemcp.in</a>. Public GitHub issue content may also be subject to GitHub's own retention and removal policies.</p></div></article>
</BaseLayout>
